  "prefLabel": "Cor 208.02 Role of Complainants in Enforcement or Disciplinary Hearings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cor 208.02 Role of Complainants in Enforcement or Disciplinary Hearings. Unless called as a witness or granted party or intervenor status, a person who initiates an adjudicative proceeding by complaining to an agency about the conduct of a person who becomes a party shall have no role in any enforcement or disciplinary hearing.\n\nSource. #9507-A, eff 7-8-09; ss by #12501, eff 3-23-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cor100-700.html"
}
